 another vector space.\n\n- Statement III is true. The set ${{c}_{3},{c}_{2},{c}_{1}}$ is a basis of ${R}^{3}$ because, by reordering the vectors, we obtain the basis $C.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only\"." 13194139533419 17592186045585 true] [17592186124873 1068 #edb/ref 17592186121808 13194139533419 17592186045585 false] [17592186124873 1068 #edb/ref 17592186318786 13194139533419 17592186045585 true] [17592186124873 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533419 17592186045585 true] [17592186124873 1071 "Let $R$ be a $8 \\cdot 12$ matrix that has $8$ pivot columns. What is the dimension of the null space of $R$?" 13194139533419 17592186045585 false] [17592186124873 1071 "Let $R$ be a $8\\times 12$ matrix that has $8$ pivot columns. What is the dimension of the null space of $R?$" 13194139533419 17592186045585 true] [17592186124873 1074 "We know that $\\text{dim(Null}(R))$ is the number of non-pivot columns in $R.$ \n\nSince $R$ has $12$ columns and $8$ of them are pivots, then the number of non-pivot columns in $R$ is \n\n$$\n12-8=4.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\text{dim(Null}(R))=4.$" 13194139533419 17592186045585 true] [17592186124874 1068 #edb/ref 17592186121814 13194139533419 17592186045585 false] [17592186124874 1068 #edb/ref 17592186318537 13194139533419 17592186045585 true] [17592186124874 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533419 17592186045585 true] [17592186124874 1071 "Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- If $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]$ then $\\text{dim(Null}(A))=0.$\n- If $B=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]$ then $\\text{dim(Null}(B))=2.$\n- If $C=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]$ then $\\text{dim(Null}(C))=1.$" 13194139533419 17592186045585 true] [17592186124874 1071 "Which of the following statements are true?\n\n1. If $A = \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}$ then $dim(Null(A)) = 0$.\n2. If $B = \\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 & 