ambda {a}_{0}{x}^{\\lambda -1}-{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }2(\\lambda +n){a}_{n}{x}^{\\lambda +n-1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 4**: Consolidate all the series into a single series that is equal to $0.$\n\nCollecting the terms for $n=0,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8({\\lambda }^{2}-\\lambda ){a}_{0}{x}^{\\lambda -1}-2\\lambda {a}_{0}{x}^{\\lambda -1} & = \\\\ (8{\\lambda }^{2}-8\\lambda -2\\lambda ){a}_{0}{x}^{\\lambda -1} & = \\\\ (8{\\lambda }^{2}-10\\lambda ){a}_{0}{x}^{\\lambda -1}. & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimilarly, collecting terms for $n\\ge 1,$ we obtain an infinite series of the form ${x}^{\\lambda -1}{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{b}_{n}(\\lambda ){x}^{n},$ for some ${b}_{n}(\\lambda ),$ $n\\ge 1.$\nTherefore, substituting into the homogeneous ODE, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(8{\\lambda }^{2}-10\\lambda ){a}_{0}{x}^{\\lambda -1}+{x}^{\\lambda -1}{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{b}_{n}(\\lambda ){x}^{n} & =0 \\\\ 2(4{\\lambda }^{2}-5\\lambda ){a}_{0}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{b}_{n}(\\lambda ){x}^{n} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 5**:  Set the coefficients of the series equal to $0.$\n\nSetting the coefficients of the $n=0$ term equal to $0$ with arbitrary ${a}_{0}\\ne 0,$ we obtain the indicial equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(4{\\lambda }^{2}-5\\lambda ){a}_{0} & =0 \\\\ 4{\\lambda }^{2}-5\\lambda  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533419 17592186045585 true] [17592186318991 1068 #edb/ref 17592186318794 13194139533419 17592186045585 true] [17592186318991 1069 "q-345183" 13194139533419 17592186045585 true] [17592186318991 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139533419 17592186045585 true] [17592186318991 1071 "$$\n{x}^{2}{y}^{″}+3x(x-3){y}^{′}-6y=0\n$$\n\nFind the indicial equation for a Frobenius series solution about the regular singular point $x=0$ of the differential equation above." 13194139533419 17592186045585 true] [17592186318991 1072 #uuid "9bcde26e-a814-5a9a-8d44-c07635ebcbd4" 13194139533419 17592186045585 true] [17592186318991 1074 "If $x=0$ is a re