gned}{y}^{′} & ={({\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{\\lambda +n})}^{′}={\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }(\\lambda +n){a}_{n}{x}^{\\lambda +n-1} \\\\ {y}^{″} & ={({\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }(\\lambda +n){a}_{n}{x}^{\\lambda +n-1})}^{′}={\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }(\\lambda +n-1)(\\lambda +n){a}_{n}{x}^{\\lambda +n-2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: Rewrite all the series in the equation so that they use the same index of summation, the powers of $x$ are the same, and the indices start at the same value.\n\nThe terms of the differential equation are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}{y}^{″} & ={x}^{2}\\cdot {\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }(\\lambda +n-1)(\\lambda +n){a}_{n}{x}^{\\lambda +n-2} \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }((\\lambda +n)^{2}-(\\lambda +n)){a}_{n}{x}^{\\lambda +n}, \\\\ -4x(x+7){y}^{′} & =(-4{x}^{2}-28x)\\cdot {\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }(\\lambda +n){a}_{n}{x}^{\\lambda +n-1} \\\\  & =-{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }4(\\lambda +n){a}_{n}{x}^{\\lambda +n+1}-{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }28(\\lambda +n){a}_{n}{x}^{\\lambda +n}, \\\\ 11y & ={\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }11{a}_{n}{x}^{\\lambda +n}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn the first sum of the ${y}^{′}$ term, we change the index of the summation by writing $m=n+1.$ This gives\n\n$$\n-4x(x+7){y}^{′}=-{\\sum }_{m=1}^{\\infty }4(\\lambda +m-1){a}_{m-1}{x}^{\\lambda +m}-{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }28(\\lambda +n){a}_{n}{x}^{\\lambda +n}.\n$$\n\nThen, replacing $m$ with $n$ (since it does not matter which letter we use) and isolating the $n=0$ term gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-4x(x+7){y}^{′} & =-{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }4(\\lambda +n-1){a}_{n-1}{x}^{\\lambda +n}-{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }28(\\lambda +n){a}_{n}{x}^{\\lambda +n} \\\\  & =-{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }4(\\lambda +n-1){a}_{n-1}{x}^{\\lambda +n}-28\\lambda {a}_{0}{x}^{\\lambda }-{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }28(\\lambda +n){a}_{n}{x}^{\\lambda +n} \\\\  & =-28\\lambda {a}_{0}{x}^{\\lambda }+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }[-4(\\lambda +n-1){a}_{n-1}-28(\\lambda +n){a}_{n}]{x}^{\\lambda +n}.\\end{aligned