ult, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{t}^{2}} & =\\frac{2}{{s}^{3}} \\\\ {L}^{-1}{L{{t}^{2}}} & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{2}{{s}^{3}}} \\\\ {t}^{2} & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{2}{{s}^{3}}} \\\\ {L}^{-1}{\\frac{2}{{s}^{3}}} & ={t}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the multiplicative property of the inverse Laplace transform, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\cdot {L}^{-1}{\\frac{2}{{s}^{3}}}={L}^{-1}{\\frac{4}{{s}^{3}}} \\\\ {L}^{-1}{\\frac{4}{{s}^{3}}}=2{t}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533419 17592186045585 true] [17592186319037 1068 #edb/ref 17592186318805 13194139533419 17592186045585 true] [17592186319037 1069 "q-345608" 13194139533419 17592186045585 true] [17592186319037 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533419 17592186045585 true] [17592186319037 1071 "Find the inverse Laplace transform for $F(s)=-\\frac{3}{2{s}^{4}}.$" 13194139533419 17592186045585 true] [17592186319037 1072 #uuid "8f3f7713-4a81-5063-9d20-6ffa6ef67943" 13194139533419 17592186045585 true] [17592186319037 1074 "From the table of Laplace transforms, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{t}^{3}} & =\\frac{3!}{{s}^{3+1}}=\\frac{6}{{s}^{4}},\\,s>0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, by applying the inverse Laplace transform to the above result, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{t}^{3}} & =\\frac{6}{{s}^{4}} \\\\ {L}^{-1}{L{{t}^{3}}} & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{6}{{s}^{4}}} \\\\ {t}^{3} & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{6}{{s}^{4}}} \\\\ {L}^{-1}{\\frac{6}{{s}^{4}}} & ={t}^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the multiplicative property of the inverse Laplace transform, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot {L}^{-1}{\\frac{6}{{s}^{4}}}={L}^{-1}{-\\frac{3}{2{s}^{4}}} \\\\ {L}^{-1}{-\\frac{3}{2{s}^{4}}}=-\\frac{1}{4}{t}^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533419 17592186045585 true] [17592186319038 1068 #edb/ref 17592186318525 13194139533419 17592186045585 true] [17592186319038 1069 "q-345614" 13194139533419 17592186045585 true] [17592186319038 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533419 17592186045585 true] [17592186319038 1071 "${L}^{-1}{\\f