refore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{8-x}{x(x-4)^{2}}=\\frac{1}{2x}-\\frac{1}{2(x-4)}+\\frac{1}{(x-4)^{2}}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate this expression term by term and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{8-x}{x(x-4)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}(\\frac{1}{2x}-\\frac{1}{2(x-4)}+\\frac{1}{(x-4)^{2}})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x-\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{1}{x-4}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{1}{(x-4)^{2}}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|\\,{|}_{1}^{2}-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-4|\\,{|}_{1}^{2}-\\frac{1}{x-4}\\,{|}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡2-\\operatorname{ln}⁡1)-\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡2-\\operatorname{ln}⁡3)-(-\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{1}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{2}+\\frac{1}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533419 17592186045585 true] [17592186319261 1068 #edb/ref 17592186318727 13194139533419 17592186045585 true] [17592186319261 1069 "q-348521" 13194139533419 17592186045585 true] [17592186319261 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533419 17592186045585 true] [17592186319261 1071 "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{2}^{5}\\frac{2-x}{{x}^{2}-12x+36}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139533419 17592186045585 true] [17592186319261 1072 #uuid "5ae593e0-851a-5fb0-b188-6070b7e5f252" 13194139533419 17592186045585 true] [17592186319261 1074 "Let's first factor the denominator of the integrand:\n\n$$\n\\frac{2-x}{{x}^{2}-12x+36}=\\frac{2-x}{(x-6)^{2}}\n$$\n\nWe must convert the integrand into a sum of partial fractions:\n\n$$\n\\frac{2-x}{(x-6)^{2}}=\\frac{A}{x-6}+\\frac{B}{(x-6)^{2}}\n$$\n\nTo determine the coefficients $A$ and $B,$ we first multiply both sides of the above equation by $(x-6)^{2}$ and get\n\n$$\n2-x=A(x-6)+B.\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=6,$ we can eliminate $A$ and solve for $B:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2-6 & =A(6-6)+B \\\\ B & =-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, plugging in $x=0$ and substituting 