peratorname{ln}⁡x}{4})(\\frac{5{ln}^{4}⁡x}{x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{ln}^{6}⁡x}{4}-5\\int \\frac{{ln}^{5}⁡x}{4x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{ln}^{6}⁡x}{4}-5I.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve for $I.$ We can ignore the constant of integration in this case, because it is insignificant for further evaluation of the definite integral.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\frac{{ln}^{6}⁡x}{4}-5I \\\\ 6I & =\\frac{{ln}^{6}⁡x}{4} \\\\ I & =\\frac{{ln}^{6}⁡x}{24}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate our definite integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{3}}\\frac{{ln}^{5}⁡x}{4x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{24}({ln}^{6}⁡x)\\,{|}_{1}^{{e}^{3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{24}({ln}^{6}⁡({e}^{3})-{ln}^{6}⁡(1)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{24}((3\\operatorname{ln}⁡e)^{6}-{0}^{6}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{24}({3}^{6}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{243}{8}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533419 17592186045585 true] [17592186319278 1068 #edb/ref 17592186318450 13194139533419 17592186045585 true] [17592186319278 1068 #edb/ref 17592186318899 13194139533419 17592186045585 true] [17592186319278 1069 "q-348637" 13194139533419 17592186045585 true] [17592186319278 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533419 17592186045585 true] [17592186319278 1071 "Given that $r(t)=⟨\\sqrt{6t-2},\\,{t}^{2}+3⟩,$ calculate $r(3).$\n\n$r(3)=⟨$\n{{field-1}} $,$\n\n{{field-2}}$⟩$" 13194139533419 17592186045585 true] [17592186319278 1072 #uuid "cb826cf4-c65a-5629-a04f-8195b481c1e2" 13194139533419 17592186045585 true] [17592186319278 1074 "We substitute $t=3$ into our function, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(3) & =⟨\\sqrt{6(3)-2},\\,{3}^{2}+3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\sqrt{16},\\,12⟩ \\\\  & =⟨4,\\,12⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533419 17592186045585 true] [17592186319279 1068 #edb/ref 17592186318631 13194139533419 17592186045585 true] [17592186319279 1068 #edb/ref 17592186318724 13194139533419 17592186045585 true] [17592186319279 1069 "q-348644" 13194139533419 17592186045585 true] [17592186319279 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 1319