a ={cos}^{2}⁡\\theta -{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta \n$$\n\nLetting $\\theta =\\frac{x}{3},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{2x}{3})={cos}^{2}\\,(\\frac{x}{3})-{sin}^{2}\\,(\\frac{x}{3}).\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into our integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-3\\pi /4}^{3\\pi /4}\\frac{1}{2}({cos}^{2}\\,(\\frac{x}{3})-{sin}^{2}\\,(\\frac{x}{3}))\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-3\\pi /4}^{3\\pi /4}\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{2x}{3})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{2x}{3})\\,{|}_{-3\\pi /4}^{3\\pi /4} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}[\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{2}{3}\\cdot \\frac{3\\pi }{4})-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{2}{3}\\cdot (-\\frac{3\\pi }{4}))] \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}[\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-\\frac{\\pi }{2})] \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}(1-(-1)) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533419 17592186045585 true] [17592186319293 1068 #edb/ref 17592186318632 13194139533419 17592186045585 true] [17592186319293 1069 "q-348724" 13194139533419 17592186045585 true] [17592186319293 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139533419 17592186045585 true] [17592186319293 1071 "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /2}(2{cos}^{2}⁡3x-2{sin}^{2}⁡3x+6x)\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139533419 17592186045585 true] [17592186319293 1072 #uuid "542465e2-8563-5f3e-ac3f-43f132e3b146" 13194139533419 17592186045585 true] [17592186319293 1074 "Here, we use the double-angle formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta ={cos}^{2}⁡\\theta -{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nLetting $\\theta =3x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡6x={cos}^{2}⁡3x-{sin}^{2}⁡3x.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into our integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /2}(2{cos}^{2}⁡3x-2{sin}^{2}⁡3x+6x)\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /2}(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡6x+6x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={(\\frac{2}{6}\\operatorname{sin}⁡6x+\\frac{6}{2}{x}^{2})|}_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & ={(\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡6x+3{x}^{2})|}_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =[\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\pi )+3{(\\frac{\\pi }{2})}^{2}]-[\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi )+3{(\\frac{\\pi }{6})}^{2}] \\\\  & =3(\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{4}-\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{36}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2{\\pi }^{2}}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533419 17592186045585 true] [17592186319294 1068 #edb/ref 17592186318601 13194139533419 17592186045585 true] [17592186319294 1069 "q-348727" 13194139533419 17592186045585 true] [17592186319294 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139533419 17592186045585 true] [17592186319294 1071 "![](images/08/0817984c94a989cc5d0801c829e9c0479c7afb30223450faea46ec486b4494c6.png)\n\nFind the area $A$ of the region in the $xy$-plane that is bounded by the curve $y=-5{cos}^{2}\\,(\\frac{x}{2})+5{sin}^{2}\\,(\\frac{x}{2})+4x+7,$ the $x$-axis and the lines $x=-\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ and $x=0,$ as shown above. Do not round the answer.\n\n$A=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139533419 17592186045585 true] [17592186319294 1072 #uuid "6c12a6bf-0854-5c5c-9be3-55c25edc3abf" 13194139533419 17592186045585 true] [17592186319294 1074 "The area of the region is given by\n\n$$\nA={\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{0}(-5{cos}^{2}\\,(\\frac{x}{2})+5{sin}^{2}\\,(\\frac{x}{2})+4x+7)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nTo calculate this integral, we use the double-angle formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x={cos}^{2}⁡x-{sin}^{2}⁡x\n$$\n\nWe can rewrite the above formula as\n\n$$\n-5\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=-5{cos}^{2}\\,(\\frac{x}{2})+5{sin}^{2}\\,(\\frac{x}{2}).\n$$\n\nHence, the area of the region is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{0}(-5{cos}^{2}\\,(\\frac{x}{2})+5{sin}^{2}\\,(\\frac{x}{2})+4x+7)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{0}(-5\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+4x+7)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(-5\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+2{x}^{2}+7x)\\,{|}_{-\\pi /2}^{0} \\\\  & =[-5\\operatorname{sin}⁡0+2(0)^{2}+7\\cdot 0]-[-5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-\\frac{\\pi }{2})+2{(-\\frac{\\pi }{2})}^{2}+7(-\\frac{\\pi }{2})] 