9 17592186045585 true] [17592186319298 1072 #uuid "7cffec36-a2c7-52a4-899d-53e87b25a49f" 13194139533419 17592186045585 true] [17592186319298 1074 "The area of the region is given by\n\n$$\nA={\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{0}(6{cos}^{2}⁡(2x)-6{sin}^{2}⁡(2x)+3x+17)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nTo calculate this integral, we use the double-angle formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x={cos}^{2}⁡x-{sin}^{2}⁡x\n$$\n\nWe can rewrite the above formula as\n\n$$\n6\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x=6{cos}^{2}⁡(2x)-6{sin}^{2}⁡(2x).\n$$\n\nHence, the area of the region is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{0}(6{cos}^{2}⁡(2x)-6{sin}^{2}⁡(2x)+3x+17)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{0}(6\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+3x+17)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x+\\frac{3}{2}{x}^{2}+17x)\\,{|}_{-\\pi /2}^{0} \\\\  & =[\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)+\\frac{3}{2}(0)^{2}+17\\cdot 0]-[\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-2\\pi )+\\frac{3}{2}{(-\\frac{\\pi }{2})}^{2}+17(-\\frac{\\pi }{2})] \\\\  & =[0+0+0]-[0+\\frac{3{\\pi }^{2}}{8}-\\frac{17\\pi }{2}] \\\\  & =[0+\\frac{17\\pi }{2}-\\frac{3{\\pi }^{2}}{8}]-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{17\\pi }{2}-\\frac{3{\\pi }^{2}}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533419 17592186045585 true] [17592186319299 1068 #edb/ref 17592186318456 13194139533419 17592186045585 true] [17592186319299 1069 "q-348735" 13194139533419 17592186045585 true] [17592186319299 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139533419 17592186045585 true] [17592186319299 1071 "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }6{cos}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139533419 17592186045585 true] [17592186319299 1072 #uuid "6fca33be-eb0b-53fc-a8bf-c96319215588" 13194139533419 17592186045585 true] [17592186319299 1074 "Here, we use the double-angle formula for cosine that involves the ${cos}^{2}⁡x$ term, given by\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x=2{cos}^{2}⁡x-1.\n$$\n\n \n\nRearranging, we have\n\n$$\n2{cos}^{2}⁡x=\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+1.\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides by $3,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n6{cos}^{2}⁡x=3(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+1).\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into our integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }6{cos}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }3(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={(\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+3x)|}_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =[\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\pi )+3\\pi ]-[\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi )+3\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{2}] \\\\  & =3\\pi -\\frac{3\\pi }{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\pi }{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533419 17592186045585 true] [17592186319300 1068 #edb/ref 17592186318823 13194139533419 17592186045585 true] [17592186319300 1069 "q-348737" 13194139533419 17592186045585 true] [17592186319300 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139533419 17592186045585 true] [17592186319300 1071 "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{-\\pi /4}^{\\pi /4}(4{cos}^{2}⁡x-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x)\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139533419 17592186045585 true] [17592186319300 1072 #uuid "6453fac7-f808-5869-802f-ea2e359c84b4" 13194139533419 17592186045585 true] [17592186319300 1074 "Here, we use the double-angle formula for cosine that involves the ${cos}^{2}⁡x$ term, given by\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x=2{cos}^{2}⁡x-1.\n$$\n\n \n\nRearranging, we have\n\n$$\n2{cos}^{2}⁡x=\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+1.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the expression $4{cos}^{2}⁡x-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x,$ we get\n\n$$\n4{cos}^{2}⁡x-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x=2(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+1)-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x=2.\n$$\n\nThus, the integral becomes\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\pi /4}^{\\pi /4}(4{cos}^{2}⁡x-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x)\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-\\pi /4}^{\\pi /4}2\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2x{|}_{-\\pi /4}^{\\pi /4} \\\\  & =2(\\frac{\\pi }{4}-(-\\frac{\\pi }{4})) \\\\  & =\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533419 17592186045585 true] [17592186319301 1068 #edb/ref 17592186318760 13194139533419 17592186045585 true] 